Here's the standard approach:

### 1. Define each theme as a `ResourceDictionary`

```xml
<!-- Resources/Themes/LightTheme.xaml -->
<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
                    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml">
    <Color x:Key="PageBackground">#FFFFFF</Color>
    <Color x:Key="TextPrimary">#1A1A1A</Color>
    <Color x:Key="AccentColor">#0078D4</Color>
</ResourceDictionary>
```

Create matching `DarkTheme.xaml` and `HighContrastTheme.xaml` with the same keys but different values.

### 2. Merge a default theme in `App.xaml`

```xml
<Application.Resources>
    <ResourceDictionary>
        <ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
            <ResourceDictionary Source="Resources/Themes/LightTheme.xaml" />
        </ResourceDictionary.MergedDictionaries>
    </ResourceDictionary>
</Application.Resources>
```

### 3. Create a theme-switching service

```csharp
public enum AppTheme { Light, Dark, HighContrast }

public static class ThemeService
{
    public static void ApplyTheme(AppTheme theme)
    {
        var mergedDicts = Application.Current!.Resources.MergedDictionaries;
        mergedDicts.Clear();

        mergedDicts.Add(theme switch
        {
            AppTheme.Dark         => new DarkTheme(),
            AppTheme.HighContrast => new HighContrastTheme(),
            _                     => new LightTheme(),
        });

        // Persist the choice
        Preferences.Set("AppTheme", theme.ToString());
    }

    public static void LoadSavedTheme()
    {
        if (Enum.TryParse<AppTheme>(Preferences.Get("AppTheme", "Light"), out var saved))
            ApplyTheme(saved);
    }
}
```

> Each `.xaml` theme file gets a code-behind class (e.g. `LightTheme`). That's what you instantiate above.

### 4. Call `LoadSavedTheme()` on startup

```csharp
// App.xaml.cs
public App()
{
    InitializeComponent();
    ThemeService.LoadSavedTheme();
}
```

### 5. Wire up the settings page

```xml
<Picker Title="Theme" SelectedIndexChanged="OnThemeChanged">
    <Picker.ItemsSource>
        <x:Array Type="{x:Type x:String}">
            <x:String>Light</x:String>
            <x:String>Dark</x:String>
            <x:String>High Contrast</x:String>
        </x:Array>
    </Picker.ItemsSource>
</Picker>
```

```csharp
void OnThemeChanged(object sender, EventArgs e)
{
    var picker = (Picker)sender;
    var theme = (AppTheme)picker.SelectedIndex;
    ThemeService.ApplyTheme(theme);
}
```

### 6. Use `DynamicResource` everywhere

```xml
<Label Text="Hello" TextColor="{DynamicResource TextPrimary}" />
<ContentPage BackgroundColor="{DynamicResource PageBackground}" />
```

**Key point:** `DynamicResource` (not `StaticResource`) is what makes the swap take effect immediately without restarting pages. Every control that references a theme color will update automatically when `MergedDictionaries` is swapped.
